column2:
Are the people in your city, with various tastes and speech, doing well? Do they not live on gifts and worn clothes?
naradapuran:139:28	Do you yourself, son, look after the elephants and horses? Do you look on all the mothers alike?
naradapuran:139:29	Do people not eat on Vishnu's day, son? When the moon has waned, does a man devote himself to shraddha?
naradapuran:139:30	Do you always give up sleep in the later watches of the night? Sleep is the root of adharma; sleep increases sin;
naradapuran:139:31	sleep produces poverty; sleep destroys welfare; a king given to sleep does not rule the earth for long;
naradapuran:139:32	like a wanton woman she always ruins both worlds of her husband. To him speaking so, the son
